    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0145" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 724.3415/26.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Bolivian Minister to the Acting Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bolivian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: I thank you very cordially
                    for the kind interest you have taken regarding my request concerning Bolivia’s
                    relations with Paraguay.</p>
                <p>I intended calling on you to inform you that the troops that have appeared in the
                    neighborhood or our forts in the vicinity of the Paraguay boundary turned out to
                    be some filibusters armed by some land speculators.</p>
                <p>The report of the American Minister at Asuncion is very gratifying, and it
                    dispels any fear that might exist as to the pacific policy of our good neighbors
                    of Paraguay. Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">I. Calderon</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
